      ":question/problem": "$$\nf(y,x)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,{{selection}}⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(y,x)$ above parametrizes the parabolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $5z=3{y}^{2}.$ What is the third component of $f?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, write the dependent coordinate as an explicit function of $y.$\n\n$$\n5z=3{y}^{2}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad z=\\frac{3}{5}{y}^{2}\n$$\n\nFor any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y,x) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x,\\,y,\\,\\frac{3}{5}{y}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $f$ is $\\frac{3}{5}{y}^{2}.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
